WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.800
Fist of the North Star, danger lurks at every turn and hits when least expected.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:28.740
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:29.680
I'm Mike.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.840
I'm Sean. And I'm Sam.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.400
What do you guys know about Fist of the North Star?

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.400
Like, does that mean anything to you?

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:38.660
Sam? Nope.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.360
Sean? Nope.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.120
Yeah, it's weird, right?

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:49.940
Like, I feel like even now, in terms of like, you know, great animes and or even mangas like,

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.060
you know, that's like, that's a big thing in our culture now.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.180
But like, I don't think Fist of the North Star gets brought up that much.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:01:01.600
However, there were 245 issues of this bad boy back in 1983, all the way through 1988.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:10.560
And, you know, it has like, there's a TV series, there's, there's movies, there's a manga, there's still video games being made.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.760
Yeah, I saw that.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:18.680
And I just think it's like, it's wild that, you know, we were getting versions like kind of like that Dragon Ball game.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:19.860
Remember that? Yeah.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:24.300
Where it was like, oh, that's weird, because nobody would have really known what Dragon Ball was.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.800
But they just, they made it in Japan, because it was popular there.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.260
And then you get these games.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:36.420
So this is the kind of thing that like, Fist of the North Star probably, you know, like airs, you know, like on Toonami in like, the 2000s.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.240
And then people are like, oh, I wonder if they ever made video games for that.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.400
And then they find out like, wait, there was an NES game, and I played it?

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.600
Like, it's kind of strange.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:53.960
Yeah, I don't know what makes, like, I guess, when it's something like the Dragon Ball game, which I don't think was called Dragon Ball.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.560
It was called Dragon Power.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:05.920
Dragon Power. Like, that's sort of a situation where it seems like they thought the game was good enough, but they knew that it wasn't going to be recognizable in the States.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.500
So they sort of like rebranded it.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:23.520
It's just weird to see that this was a property that was, what I'm imagining is virtually unknown in the West, and they keep all the branding, and they keep all of like the context around the show that nobody's seen.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:25.560
So I found that odd.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:30.760
Yeah, and yet there's not like, there's not a lot of story to digest, definitely not in the game itself.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:35.440
But, you know, I feel like even the manual, you don't need to have any prior knowledge.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:42.520
And in fact, the Famicom version of this game, which, you know, I keep saying Famicom because it did come to Japan first.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:47.200
Like, that one wasn't even trying to tell like the full story.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:51.680
It was just telling like a few selected issues of Fist of the North Star.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:53.960
So I don't think you really needed to know anything.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:56.380
You guys didn't feel like you were missing out, right, on any deep lore?

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:02.920
I found it odd though, like, that everything was so specific.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.480
Like, the names of the levels.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:18.200
I guess it's really just the names of the levels, where there are references to armies and generals and a concentration camp or something like that.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:29.460
And I just, I think that if it just removed all of those like specific names, then this wouldn't have felt more like a non sequitur.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.180
I don't know if you kind of get what I'm saying.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:38.860
Yeah, it's, it's kind of like if, you know, Kung Fu, one of those early 1985 games we played.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:47.160
It'd be like if you found out that like, you know, Sylvia and all that stuff like was actually a story in the manga, but you never read that book.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.840
So you can still play the game.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:53.840
Right. And there's things that's like, oh, I guess that's a reference.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:04:02.520
But if it, I don't know, it's like it's, it's specific enough to that someone would tell me it's a reference and I believe them.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.700
But also, I feel like we're in a time where these games kind of have weird shit in them anyway.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:16.940
Yeah. So if there's like a something oddly specific, I just kind of roll with it and don't really think anything else of it.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:25.720
And it also depends on what you know about Fist of the North Star, because the game also took a lot of liberties in terms of plot for people who are familiar with the content.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.380
So forget about us who have no idea.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:32.300
It's funny to think that like you could have read all the manga and you would be like, wait, who's this?

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:42.980
Because the four generals that you fight in the game, one of them's from the manga, two are exclusive to the anime, and one is brand new just for the game.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.980
So you don't really need to know that much.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.640
Yeah, I guess this is just a whole cluster then.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:54.560
But if you are wondering what Fist of the North Star is, it is set on a post-apocalyptic Earth after a nuclear war.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:05:00.380
And a warrior named Kenshiro has this like, he knows your vital points.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:10.360
It's this martial arts thing where he can, he touches a specific spot and it, all of his enemies die in like incredibly gruesome manners.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:11.720
That's like, it's very funny.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:16.660
You know, it's like ridiculous over the top, you know, oh, that his weak point is in his shoulder.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:18.820
And then, you know, the result is just ridiculous.

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:29.100
But he's fighting against like, just, you know, normal post-apocalyptic stuff like, you know, gangs and bandits that have like taken over society.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.520
And now he's trying to like protect the innocent.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.000
And I was like, I don't know if that's enough.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.360
Like, you know, it's a pretty like broad stroke plot.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:37.760
So I'm sure they get into more detail.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:40.600
But I don't know if that's enough for 245 issues.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:45.820
How much of this did you read slash watch?

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:50.660
I watched a good amount because that was, the visuals are good.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:53.800
You know, if you like, I'm not saying it's, it's like Toriyama's Dragon Ball.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:55.900
But like, if you're familiar with that era, it's fine.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.860
It's cozy to watch those kinds of shows.

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:04.320
But I also did have to like go to Wikipedia just to find out like who's who and stuff like that.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:07.380
Not that we're going to break down the course here or anything like that.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:11.040
Because the plot in the game is, is kind of similar.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:17.380
It's just, you know, you're Kenshiro and you're just trying to take down like a couple different imperial forces.

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:20.220
Like, I think there's like four generals that I mentioned.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:26.700
And you're just trying to, you know, go one to the next and using your special martial arts powers.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:28.720
And I don't think you need to really know anything beyond that.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:31.160
Yeah, it's also funny.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:37.180
This, this may be a little off topic, but you know, we, we really haven't talked about the game much yet.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:45.140
And I think that if somebody started playing, uh, when they started the podcast, they might already be like a quarter of the way through the game.

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:56.180
Okay. Yeah. So let's, let's talk about that for a second, not even just the length, but like, this is a game where I feel like for once we are actually powerful from the get go.

00:06:56.340 --> 00:07:04.520
Like I felt strong as the character and I've, I enjoyed playing as Kenshiro, if only because it was kind of playing on an easy game.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.720
Yeah. This was a very easy game.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:16.060
Um, which really, which really struck me as odd because of just the, uh, the density of Nintendo hard games that we've been playing.

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:18.040
Um, yeah.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:20.920
How did, was this a single session for you guys?

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:22.680
Yeah. Yeah.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:26.680
And just to set it up too, for everybody, it's a side scrolling beat them up.

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:32.000
So as you can imagine with your karate stuff, like you just have your sets of punches and kicks.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:39.980
However, you know, there's a, when you kill certain enemies, they leave behind stars that you can get powers for, and then you power up.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:48.440
And that allows you to do like even more incredible feats, uh, not with any extra button inputs or anything like that, but that's the general, like, gist of the game.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:57.520
So otherwise you're just kind of coming up upon enemies who are, forgive me, you know, forgive me if I'm wrong guys, but like, is it not one hit KO for almost everything other than sub bosses?

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:00.460
No, I mean, some of them take a couple of hits.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:05.420
I think unless I, unless it takes so long to die that I can't tell that it's only one hit.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:06.560
Or if you just miss.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:09.960
Yeah. I wasn't sure if I was missing or if I was, or if it was one hit.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:12.260
Yeah. So yeah.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:16.760
Cause there's something like, yeah, the, the punches and the kicks, like when you hit those guys, they go flying.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.320
Yeah. Yeah.

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:23.620
There are some that go flying and some just sort of stand there and then evaporate into stars.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:29.080
But, uh, that, that, that's sort of a, uh, a mechanic that I never fully understood, but.

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:30.060
That's how I want to go.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:55.040
So it's good that you're powerful in the game and everything like that.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:09:00.320
And I think it's great that all three of us were able to play this in a single session, a rare thing, uh, for us.

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:01.380
We're not good at NES games.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:05.000
Let's just be honest. But did that translate.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:06.740
Does easy mean fun?

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:08.520
No, you know what?

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:15.900
The only reason that like, it was like, yeah, I'm glad that we all got this in a single session because we're doing this for work pretty much.

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:24.440
But I'd be pissed if I bought this game for full price and got one game out of it, like one sit down.

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:28.580
And I didn't even get yelled at by my mom to come to dinner.

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:31.820
Yeah. I, I don't know.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.040
I mean, I guess jumping is a little fun, right?

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:39.880
We'll talk about that jump, Sam, because he like, it's not really a jump, right?

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:40.760
That's like a leap.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.880
Yeah. It's like an anti-gravity kind of jump.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:48.100
Like you can do a normal jump if you just tap the jump button.

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:53.880
But if you hold it down a little bit more, you just kind of levitate upwards diagonally.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.480
And it's, I think it's the fastest way of moving also.

00:09:57.880 --> 00:09:58.740
Yeah, it is.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:03.420
Yeah, I would constantly jump. So Sam, you mentioned the tap jump button, right?

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:07.960
And I, I noticed that by like mistake, but there's no reason to ever do that, right?

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:09.540
I mean. I don't think so.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.000
I guess not.

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:23.440
I mean, there are some like tight corners that if you want to take advantage of the, the faster movement speed of the jump where like you can't really get too big of a jump off, maybe you would do that.

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:29.880
But other than that, it's just a quirk of the fact that, that a jump just lasts as long as you hold the button down.

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:39.420
Or if you just want to time your next big jump, you know, you see an obstacle coming up and you know that if you do two big jumps, you will, you'll hit the front of it.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:42.680
But if you do a little jump and a big jump, then you'll just clear it.

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:45.440
But that's the only jump algebra.

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:51.380
Yeah. And, you know, usually we complain about enemies spawning all over the place.

00:10:51.700 --> 00:11:00.640
This one has that problem where enemies that you just defeated will just spawn back in again if you kind of like hang out or, or turn in the wrong direction.

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:05.920
However, they give you only ever like one or two at a time and it's never really like unmanageable.

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:08.580
There are some later on that get projectiles.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:13.400
But I feel, I feel like they were kind of fair with how fast the projectiles come at you.

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:17.020
And since your jump is so large, like timing's not really an issue.

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:21.880
It's just, it's weird to get things that you want and then see why you shouldn't want them.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:25.040
No, this is just the complete opposite end of the spectrum.

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:29.020
Like, yeah, they're not really like, they're not hand placed.

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:33.540
Some of them may be hand placed, but I'm sure that like some of them just spam randomly.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:43.580
But all of the enemies aside from mini bosses and the bosses themselves are so impotent that it really doesn't matter that it's just sort of scattershot.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:53.240
I don't, like, wish that there were more enemies just because they're so easy to take down that I feel like to really feel like a super powerful person,

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:56.760
they should just give us waves and waves of them in some places.

00:11:57.260 --> 00:12:00.220
Just smack them all down in one hit, you know?

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:13.820
Yeah, that's a different kind of beat-em-up that I think we're used to in arcade games where, like, you know, you can't progress forward until you clear off, like, a section of, you know, of enemies.

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:21.380
And that never happens here because they've designed, you know, this, I'm not going to call it a labyrinth.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:26.820
It's not very, you know, it's not like you have to actually, like, navigate yourself around these things.

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:32.340
However, there is places to go and, you know, you have to kind of think about, like, you know, have I been here before?

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:36.160
Like, maybe I, you know, the directions and stuff like that and you have to go through doors.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:53.720
So I feel like that's why they didn't do the, like, bring on the enemies in waves because you're just kind of, like, or at least the game's focus is more about you figuring out where you need to go while making it not that complicated.

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:58.380
Yeah. This really is a weird game.

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:08.880
It feels like, like, midway through the game, maybe, I don't know, maybe level two or three, they're like, oh, this would be a great, like, Metroidvania sort of thing.

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:18.540
And they did, like, one or two branching paths and then they kind of dropped that whole thing and everything else.

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:24.040
Maybe that was, like, the theme for that particular, like, issue in the manga, right?

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:25.520
Like, maybe that was a thing.

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:27.860
Like, he was, you know. Oh, he goes upstairs, yes.

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:29.360
Right, yeah, yeah. And downstairs.

00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:34.300
Or he has to, like, infiltrate an enemy base or something like that and they're trying to, like, go for that.

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:44.440
However, I think that that, like, hindered the game more because they started focusing on, like, your navigation and exploring without making it, like, you know, it's kind of empty.

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:47.700
There's really nothing to explore anyway, so why even bother with stuff like that?

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:56.840
I guess that adding the time limit to it kind of adds an element of gameplay that is, like, now you gotta figure it out fast.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:14:01.600
Like, not only do you have to survive, but you have to figure out where you're going before the time runs out.

00:14:01.780 --> 00:14:04.200
So, I don't know.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:10.760
Because I got to the, that boss of the staircase level with one second left.

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:12.820
And I, it felt, that felt kind of cool.

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:15.840
Oh, does the clock reset once you hit the boss?

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:21.440
Or? Yeah, it gives you, it gives you more time when you hit the, like, the mini boss and the main boss.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:22.500
Oh, I see.

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:28.020
Yeah, I think it also was sort of a, to temper, like, farming for stars.

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:37.600
Maybe, maybe it's not possible, but it definitely seemed possible to just sort of, like, hang out and try and get stars from killing random enemies.

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:44.420
Um, so maybe that was there so you couldn't just be level 10 stars on the first screen.

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:45.440
But, I don't know.

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:09.820
The power meter, uh, which is the thing that you use to collect stars, it raises your power meter.

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:18.720
That is kind of cool, though, uh, that, you know, without, without, um, requiring different power-ups or, you know, making it into a Metroidvania.

00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:21.720
Just making you stronger as you continue to collect powers.

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:29.720
I, I liked the one where all of a sudden you can just, like, hold down the attack buttons and then you just do rapid punching and rapid kicking.

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:31.140
Is that not how it is?

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:33.300
I thought that was just, it started out that way.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.180
I don't think it starts out that way.

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:40.300
Huh. Because, uh, on the list of power-ups I have here, that's listed as one of them.

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:43.060
I mean, maybe, but, um, it's listed as one of them.

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:45.560
So maybe it's faster. Maybe it does, like, double damage or something.

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:50.980
Yeah, I guess for a while I was just sort of tapping because I didn't, I didn't know that that existed yet.

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:53.480
Yeah, there's some other cool stuff, though.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:57.320
Uh, there's a, a projectile, like, uh, what do you want to call that?

00:15:57.420 --> 00:15:58.440
Is that, like, a key blast?

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:00.340
They call them bombs. Bombs, okay.

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:02.260
I was thinking, like, again, Dragon Ball.

00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:05.100
Ha ha ha. Oh, key.

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:06.640
That kind of thing. Yeah, yeah.

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:10.440
And then there's, like, other power-ups that are like, okay, now you can walk faster.

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.480
And it's like, eh, I think we could have thought of something.

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:15.080
For a martial arts guy, I think we could have thought of something a little better.

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:17.720
I like the one where you're two people.

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:22.520
Oh, yeah. And, but, but it's, like, you're just the guy who's in front, really.

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:28.540
Because when you change directions, like, it flips, it flips you.

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:33.000
So the, whoever won't, like, they're, sorry, I'm not explaining this well.

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:41.260
If there's two people facing the right, if you turn left, then the guy who was furthest

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:43.640
right stays in the same spot and just turns left.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:47.700
And the guy that was furthest left is now all the way on your right and is, like, flipped

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:48.740
over to the other side.

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:54.960
Yeah, it looks like it's supposed to be a kind of, like, oh, you do, like, double damage.

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:59.420
You could fight, like, two guys at once if they're at this very specific distance apart.

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:01.960
But it ends up just being, like, an invincibility.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:08.040
And it almost feels like the fact that there are two of you, it looks like a bug.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:13.020
But maybe that's just, like, oh, he's moving so fast that you see double and you can't touch it.

00:17:13.020 --> 00:17:14.820
I thought it was a bug at first.

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:21.620
Yeah. It's, like, one of those things that you see in anime sometimes where it looks cooler than

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:23.340
it really is, like Super Saiyan 3.

00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:26.060
Oh, the hair? Yeah.

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:27.340
The hair is so cool.

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:28.580
Yeah, the hair is cool.

